From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cepvor <cepvor@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AOSCOS: cmake: do not enable SVE/SVE2 from the build host

FindSVE.cmake and FindSVE2.cmake decide whether to build SVE
primitives by reading the build host's /proc/cpuinfo. When the host
has SVE, source/CMakeLists.txt adds "-march=armv8-a+sve2" (or "+sve")
to ARM_ARGS through add_definitions(). That option ends up at the end
of every compile command line and overrides the baseline
"-march=armv8-a" a distribution build passes in, so the objects
contain SVE instructions and crash with SIGILL on any aarch64 machine
without SVE.

SVE is optional in ARMv8.2-A, and consumer SoCs such as the
Snapdragon 8cx Gen 3 do not implement it. Building x265 on a host with
SVE therefore produces a package that does not work on most arm64
systems it will be installed on. The failure is also easy to miss:
through ffmpeg (libx265) it looks like a silent failure with a
zero-byte output and exit status 0, and only running the x265 CLI
directly shows "Illegal instruction". The core dump points at the SVE
"cntd" instruction.

Follow the approach of
0003-AOSCOS-cmake-only-specify-necessary-flags-for-ARM-op.patch and
put the probe results behind explicit options that default to OFF, so
a distribution build only targets the baseline ISA. Users who do want
SVE/SVE2 can still turn it on with -DENABLE_SVE=ON / -DENABLE_SVE2=ON.
The CROSS_COMPILE_SVE and CROSS_COMPILE_SVE2 variables keep working
unchanged, so cross-compilation workflows that set them are unaffected.

x265 4.3 adds runtime feature detection (RTFD) upstream and picks the
implementation at load time instead, at the cost of linking in every
optimisation variant:
https://x265.readthedocs.io/en/master/releasenotes.html
Until the package is updated to that release, defaulting the options
to OFF keeps the build portable.

Signed-off-by: Cepvor <cepvor@qq.com>
---
 source/CMakeLists.txt | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/CMakeLists.txt b/source/CMakeLists.txt
index 0d703ab..2d0c1f2 100755
--- a/source/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/source/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -260,9 +260,24 @@ if(GCC)
         endif()
     endif()
 	if(ARM64 OR CROSS_COMPILE_ARM64)
+        # find_package(SVE) and find_package(SVE2) below check the build
+        # host's /proc/cpuinfo. A distribution build must not copy build-host
+        # features into the binary: a library built on a host with SVE
+        # contains SVE instructions and crashes with SIGILL on targets that
+        # lack SVE. SVE is optional in ARMv8.2-A, and most consumer aarch64
+        # SoCs do not implement it. Put the probe results behind an explicit
+        # option; CROSS_COMPILE_SVE/SVE2 still work as before.
+        option(ENABLE_SVE "Build SVE primitives (requires SVE on the target CPU)" OFF)
+        option(ENABLE_SVE2 "Build SVE2 primitives (requires SVE2 on the target CPU)" OFF)
         find_package(Neon)
         find_package(SVE)
         find_package(SVE2)
+        if(NOT ENABLE_SVE)
+            set(CPU_HAS_SVE 0)
+        endif()
+        if(NOT ENABLE_SVE2)
+            set(CPU_HAS_SVE2 0)
+        endif()
         if(CPU_HAS_SVE2 OR CROSS_COMPILE_SVE2)
             message(STATUS "Found SVE2")
 	        set(ARM_ARGS -O3 -march=armv8-a+sve2 -fPIC -flax-vector-conversions)
-- 
